ined residue identified is /tmp/benchmark-reboot.log, created for reboot command output and not cleaned afterward. No other unnecessary mutations are established by the trace.","evidence_ids":["cmd-fae2367e2a834f3c","cmd-773d016e0ab44fe1","cmd-120cbd0f446e4c69","cmd-b1a74b322b234dde","cmd-ca2b7797ae624869","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. Node1 presents a CA-signed SSH host certificate, and a strict client trusts it solely through an @cert-authority entry without a pinned host key. The configuration and behavior also survived the independently required node restart.","limitations":["The lifecycle snapshots do not inventory /etc/ssh or /root, so persistence of those files is established by the direct post-reboot commands rather than by the supplemental snapshots.","The authorized_keys command was conditional, so the trace does not establish whether that file was actually modified; no hygiene penalty is inferred for it."]}
